// ch11 (round 2, R2-2 / #2227): the .vibex rows of the require-pin
// lane table. The same pin line p31 carries in a .vibe answers
// DIFFERENTLY on every lane once the file is a .vibex:
//   - compile lane / `vibe run`: `unknown # directive: pkg` (the
//     script-head directive scan reads the pin's `#pkg:sha1:` as a
//     `#` directive);
//   - `vibe check`: `unexpected token: =` at the pin line.
// When #2227 lands, all lanes should accept it, as the .vibe build
// lane already does.
//! cli: run
//! cli: check
require @vibe/core 0.2.0 = #pkg:sha1:0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

fn main with Console {
  println("pin head parsed")
}
